WEBVTT

00:17.107 --> 00:22.437
<b>THE ELUSIVE SAMURAI</b>

01:32.257 --> 01:35.427
<b>Now, then. Today I shall tell you the tale</b>

01:36.267 --> 01:40.767
<b>of a certain young lord
whose greatest talent is running away.</b>

01:44.187 --> 01:47.357
<b>The year is 1333.</b>

01:48.357 --> 01:51.237
<b>The Kamakura shogunate,
which had established rule by the samurai,</b>

01:51.327 --> 01:55.077
<b>fell because of the rebellion
of its vassal, Takauji Ashikaga.</b>

01:55.577 --> 01:58.497
<b>Having lost everything,
the rightful heir, Tokiyuki Hojo,</b>

01:58.577 --> 02:03.877
<b>flees to Suwa under the guidance of
the Shinto priest, Yorishige Suwa,</b>

02:03.957 --> 02:07.257
<b>where he and his companions
begin gathering the strength</b>

02:07.337 --> 02:08.427
<b>to reclaim Kamakura.</b>

02:10.467 --> 02:12.387
<b>One year later…</b>

02:13.467 --> 02:15.637
<b>After experiencing his first battle
at Kawanakajima in northern Shinano,</b>

02:15.717 --> 02:17.807
<b>Tokiyuki renews his resolve
to face this turbulent age</b>

02:17.887 --> 02:23.767
<b>through "running away" and "surviving."</b>

02:26.147 --> 02:31.407
<b>How will this game of tag
to reclaim the throne end?</b>

02:31.907 --> 02:33.947
<b>What fate awaits Tokiyuki?</b>

02:34.027 --> 02:36.537
<b>Don't miss what comes next!</b>

02:39.287 --> 02:41.037
<b>What a pain. I hate guard duty.</b>

02:41.117 --> 02:42.707
<b>1334 - TAKEDA CLAN TERRITORY
(KAI GENJI)</b>

02:42.787 --> 02:44.957
<b>It appears the remnants of the Hojo clan
who fled Kamakura</b>

02:45.047 --> 02:47.207
<b>are stirring up rebellions
all over the place.</b>

02:47.297 --> 02:49.127
<b>They could be hiding around here too.</b>

02:50.087 --> 02:54.597
<b>I heard they couldn't even coordinate,
and most of them got wiped out.</b>

02:54.677 --> 02:57.927
<b>There aren't any Hojo left.</b>

02:58.017 --> 02:59.427
<b>-Huh?
-What?</b>

02:59.517 --> 03:03.107
<b>The brats are back!</b>

03:03.767 --> 03:05.687
<b>ONE DAY EARLIER</b>

03:05.767 --> 03:07.937
<b>Big Brother, how are the locusts?</b>

03:08.567 --> 03:11.987
<b>I'm getting used to them. It reminds me
of the sakura shrimp in Suruga Bay.</b>

03:15.447 --> 03:16.447
<b>Come to think of it,</b>

03:16.537 --> 03:19.617
<b>I'd like to know what
my lord's meals were like in Kamakura.</b>

03:19.707 --> 03:21.707
<b>They must have been quite lavish.</b>

03:22.617 --> 03:25.627
<b>Delicacies I've never even seen before…</b>

03:26.547 --> 03:30.257
<b>Not really. Most of the time, it wasn't
much different from everyone else's.</b>

03:31.877 --> 03:33.677
<b>But my favorite was sea bream.</b>

03:33.757 --> 03:35.177
<b>SEA BREAM?</b>

03:35.257 --> 03:36.257
<b>Sea bream?</b>

03:36.347 --> 03:38.597
<b><i>Kamakura is by the sea,</i></b>

03:38.677 --> 03:41.847
<b><i>so fish caught that morning at Yuigahama</i>
<i>would be served by noon.</i></b>

03:42.517 --> 03:47.187
<b><i>You eat thinly-sliced sea bream</i>
<i>topped with Izu wasabi and hishio.</i></b>

03:47.767 --> 03:51.277
<b>It was so fresh, and had such
a great texture, I couldn't stop eating.</b>

03:52.197 --> 03:54.067
<b>I wish I could have it again.</b>

03:56.947 --> 03:59.947
<b>He seemed down.</b>

04:00.037 --> 04:02.287
<b>He must be missing Kamakura.</b>

04:03.037 --> 04:06.377
<b>I wish there was something
we could do for him.</b>

04:08.587 --> 04:10.007
<b>Sea bream is my dream!</b>

04:13.007 --> 04:18.757
<b>Fresh sea bream with great texture is my…</b>

04:20.347 --> 04:22.017
<b>-…drea--
-We're in Shinano!</b>

04:22.097 --> 04:24.687
<b>There's no way anyone could bring
fresh sea bream all the way here…</b>

04:25.977 --> 04:26.977
<b>My lord?</b>

04:34.607 --> 04:36.987
<b><i>This is the second summer</i>
<i>since Kamakura was destroyed…</i></b>

04:37.617 --> 04:39.617
<b><i>Looking from my second home, Suwa,</i></b>

04:39.697 --> 04:42.577
<b><i>my first home lies beyond Mount Fuji,</i>
<i>off to the left.</i></b>

04:43.957 --> 04:46.627
<b><i>I want to go back to Kamakura.</i></b>

04:50.047 --> 04:51.047
<b>Sea bream is my…</b>

04:55.297 --> 04:56.297
<b>Huh?</b>

04:56.387 --> 04:58.177
<b>Stop! You're entering Takeda terri--</b>

04:58.717 --> 05:01.347
<b>Shut up! We don't have time!
We're coming through!</b>

05:01.427 --> 05:03.017
<b>I can see the ocean!</b>

05:04.977 --> 05:08.647
<b>Genba, you and I will head east.
Ayako, head west.</b>

05:09.567 --> 05:10.857
<b>Got it!</b>

05:10.937 --> 05:13.277
<b>Kojiro, you guys get the ice
from the ice chamber.</b>

05:13.357 --> 05:15.987
<b>Bury it right away
to keep it from melting.</b>

05:16.067 --> 05:17.067
<b>Yeah, got it!</b>

05:17.157 --> 05:19.027
<b>See you back here!</b>

05:19.947 --> 05:23.077
<b>Shizuku and the others
won't be back until sunrise tomorrow.</b>

05:23.657 --> 05:27.497
<b>Let's practice so we can kill
our prized prey at the exact moment.</b>

05:29.747 --> 05:32.417
<b>Kojiro, let's go for a long ride.</b>

05:33.547 --> 05:35.467
<b>I'm sorry, young lord.</b>

05:35.967 --> 05:39.217
<b>Kojiro is away on an errand
for a few days.</b>

05:39.297 --> 05:40.297
<b>I see.</b>

05:42.057 --> 05:43.057
<b>Shizuku?</b>

05:45.267 --> 05:46.347
<b>Ayako?</b>

05:49.187 --> 05:50.267
<b>Nobody's here.</b>

05:52.107 --> 05:54.687
<b>Yorishige is here.</b>

05:54.777 --> 05:56.857
<b>We shall practice the flute today.</b>

06:09.497 --> 06:10.497
<b>We've got a bite!</b>

06:11.747 --> 06:12.957
<b>Where is everyone?</b>

06:16.007 --> 06:17.297
<b>-Here they are!
-Now!</b>

06:19.127 --> 06:20.757
<b>-Your way, Kojiro!
-I see it!</b>

06:20.837 --> 06:23.927
<b><i>If a fish thrashes around on the ground,</i>
<i>it won't stay fresh.</i></b>

06:24.007 --> 06:25.967
<b><i>Sever the brain and the artery</i></b>

06:26.057 --> 06:27.767
<b>while it's still… in the air!</b>

06:30.647 --> 06:32.897
<b>Nice catch!</b>

06:32.977 --> 06:34.147
<b>What about the Izu wasabi?</b>

06:34.227 --> 06:35.527
<b>Bought it fresh!</b>

06:35.607 --> 06:36.777
<b>Good. Let's head back.</b>

06:36.857 --> 06:38.777
<b>From here on,
we don't have a moment to spare.</b>

06:39.397 --> 06:41.317
<b><i>Bleed the fish, remove the gills and guts,</i></b>

06:41.407 --> 06:44.077
<b><i>wrap it in cloth to keep it dry,</i>
<i>and pack it in ice.</i></b>

06:45.987 --> 06:48.157
<b>Hey, wait! There's no road!</b>

06:52.327 --> 06:54.167
<b>Oh, no! Now, there's a river!</b>

06:59.007 --> 07:00.007
<b>We'll make our own path!</b>

07:00.087 --> 07:02.137
<b>We go straight through
the shortest route, no matter what!</b>

07:02.217 --> 07:03.217
<b>FISH-TAIL LINE</b>

07:03.297 --> 07:04.887
<b><i>In an age before trains or cars,</i></b>

07:04.967 --> 07:07.307
<b><i>the Fish-Tail Line</i>
<i>marked the farthest point inland</i></b>

07:07.387 --> 07:10.137
<b><i>that fresh sea fish could be transported</i>
<i>without spoiling.</i></b>

07:10.227 --> 07:11.227
<b>SUWA
KOFU</b>

07:11.307 --> 07:13.857
<b><i>From the Pacific coast,</i>
<i>the Fish-Tail Line reached as far as Kofu.</i></b>

07:13.937 --> 07:17.527
<b><i>Beyond that, in Suwa, sea fish would spoil</i>
<i>before it could be eaten.</i></b>

07:17.607 --> 07:18.607
<b><i>Which means…</i></b>

07:18.687 --> 07:21.487
<b>The brats are back!</b>

07:21.567 --> 07:23.487
<b><i>Bringing fresh, firm sea bream</i>
<i>all the way to Suwa</i></b>

07:23.567 --> 07:24.827
<b><i>during the summer in a time of war…</i></b>

07:25.407 --> 07:26.787
<b>Kill them this time!</b>

07:26.867 --> 07:30.207
<b>Hi-yah!</b>

07:31.247 --> 07:33.327
<b><i>…was a near-impossible mission.</i></b>

07:40.757 --> 07:43.677
<b>We're back. We just went fishing.</b>

07:44.177 --> 07:46.347
<b>That was fun!</b>

07:46.427 --> 07:47.507
<b>Are you all right?</b>

07:47.597 --> 07:50.267
<b>It looks more like the aftermath
of a battle than a fishing trip.</b>

07:50.347 --> 07:52.597
<b>Since when do fish shoot arrows?</b>

07:53.097 --> 07:57.607
<b>Big Brother, I know it's a little early,
but dinner's ready.</b>

07:58.937 --> 08:01.237
<b>Please, come this way.</b>

08:01.857 --> 08:03.107
<b>Okay.</b>

08:13.457 --> 08:17.787
<b>Hey! What are you doing? That was mine!</b>

08:18.587 --> 08:21.877
<b>Oh, sorry.
You didn't seem to be eating it.</b>

08:21.967 --> 08:26.597
<b>I was saving it!
You know sea bream is my favorite!</b>

08:26.677 --> 08:29.847
<b>Was it? Well, here.</b>

08:30.767 --> 08:32.267
<b>Lotus root?</b>

08:32.347 --> 08:34.187
<b>You're just giving me what you don't like!</b>

08:34.267 --> 08:37.767
<b>Give me back my sea bream! My sea bream!</b>

08:39.647 --> 08:41.357
<b>I was just kidding.</b>

08:42.027 --> 08:43.947
<b>Here. This should do, right?</b>

08:44.697 --> 08:46.367
<b>Huh? This much?</b>

08:46.447 --> 08:48.277
<b>I'm already full.</b>

08:52.657 --> 08:55.577
<b>You're so dramatic.
You're actually crying.</b>

09:00.667 --> 09:01.667
<b>MISSION ACCOMPLISHED!!!</b>

09:01.757 --> 09:04.007
<b>Look. He's so happy he's crying.</b>

09:04.507 --> 09:07.587
<b>Is sea bream really that good?</b>

09:07.677 --> 09:08.757
<b>You guys…</b>

09:11.967 --> 09:15.727
<b><i>I'm so grateful they went all the way</i>
<i>to the sea just to catch that for me.</i></b>

09:16.397 --> 09:18.227
<b><i>How could I ever repay them?</i></b>

09:19.267 --> 09:21.647
<b>So, how long would it take
to reach Kamakura?</b>

09:22.647 --> 09:25.487
<b>With a group this small, it'd take a day.</b>

09:25.567 --> 09:29.487
<b>But Takeda of the Takauji faction
has built many new forts.</b>

09:30.447 --> 09:35.287
<b>Getting a large army through would take
20 times longer and cost many lives.</b>

09:36.037 --> 09:38.127
<b>Good work on the reconnaissance mission.</b>

09:38.917 --> 09:42.587
<b>As I thought, attacking Kamakura
by the shortest route won't be easy.</b>

09:43.207 --> 09:44.207
<b>-You went to…
-Huh?</b>

09:46.007 --> 09:47.127
<b>Kamakura?</b>

09:47.217 --> 09:51.677
<b>It's time we start working
on a concrete plan to retake Kamakura.</b>

09:56.137 --> 09:58.807
<b>Shizuku, what was Kamakura like?</b>

09:58.897 --> 10:01.357
<b>TADAYOSHI ASHIKAGA
REBUILD KAMAKURA</b>

10:01.437 --> 10:03.147
<b>Yes. It had changed dramatically.</b>

10:03.227 --> 10:05.067
<b>Under the new ruler
and the elite warriors he had assembled,</b>

10:05.147 --> 10:11.577
<b>Kamakura was abuzz with rumors
about these young warriors.</b>

10:12.327 --> 10:16.747
<b>There is no doubt they'll stand in our way
when we move to retake Kamakura.</b>

10:17.287 --> 10:22.127
<b>Interesting. I've only ever fought
old men. This will be a nice change.</b>

10:22.207 --> 10:24.957
<b>Let's make this a showdown
between the next generation.</b>

10:25.837 --> 10:30.137
<b>What do you think of that, Lord Tokiyuki?</b>

10:30.637 --> 10:34.637
<b>I've got youth on my side.
After all, I'm only nine.</b>

10:35.597 --> 10:41.057
<b>No matter how strong they are,
no one can match my devotion to Kamakura.</b>

10:42.477 --> 10:45.397
<b><i>I will take Kamakura back, no matter what!</i></b>

10:47.817 --> 10:52.777
<b><i>Compared to the days of Hojo, the new</i>
<i>rulers of Kamakura were much younger.</i></b>

10:53.367 --> 10:56.997
<b><i>After being assigned</i>
<i>to devastated Kamakura,</i></b>

10:57.077 --> 11:00.167
<b><i>Tadayoshi Ashikaga simultaneously</i>
<i>pushed forward the city's reconstruction</i></b>

11:00.247 --> 11:03.087
<b><i>and the restoration of public order.</i></b>

11:03.167 --> 11:05.127
<b><i>To carry out his will,</i>
<i>he established the Kanto Hisashiban.</i></b>

11:05.207 --> 11:06.207
<b>RAWR</b>

11:06.297 --> 11:08.917
<b><i>Tadayoshi left his seasoned retainers</i>
<i>in Kyo with Takauji.</i></b>

11:09.007 --> 11:10.217
<b><i>He formed the Kanto Hisashiban</i></b>

11:10.297 --> 11:13.427
<b><i>from promising young men who would</i>
<i>carry the future of the Ashikaga clan.</i></b>

11:13.507 --> 11:14.507
<b>No!</b>

11:14.597 --> 11:16.427
<b>GROUP 1 LEADER, KANTO HISASHIBAN
YOSHISUE SHIBUKAWA (20)</b>

11:16.517 --> 11:17.517
<b>How disgraceful.</b>

11:17.597 --> 11:19.017
<b>Some of them
owe the Hojo a great debt of gratitude,</b>

11:19.097 --> 11:21.187
<b>yet they're shamelessly fawning.</b>

11:21.267 --> 11:23.107
<b>GROUP 2 LEADER, KANTO HISASHIBAN
TSUNEIE IWAMATSU (?)</b>

11:23.187 --> 11:24.767
<b>Don't be such a stick-in-the-mud,
Shibukawa.</b>

11:24.857 --> 11:27.897
<b>A good wave and a beautiful woman,
never let either pass you by.</b>

11:27.987 --> 11:29.987
<b>GROUP 2 VICE-LEADER, KANTO
HISASHIBAN NORIAKI UESUGI (28)</b>

11:30.067 --> 11:31.407
<b>My, how frightening, Mr. Iwamatsu.</b>

11:31.487 --> 11:34.907
<b>Talking about women
in front of Lord Tadayoshi, of all people.</b>

11:34.987 --> 11:36.737
<b>ASSISTANT, KANTO HISASHIBAN
MAGOJIRO SHIBA (13)</b>

11:36.827 --> 11:38.867
<b>Lord Tadayoshi isn't as uptight
as he used to be.</b>

11:38.947 --> 11:41.037
<b>He even lets us dress however we like.</b>

11:41.117 --> 11:43.287
<b>No, I'm still as uptight as ever.</b>

11:43.377 --> 11:44.457
<b>You are?</b>

11:45.207 --> 11:48.457
<b>If this were Kyo, I'd make them
mind their manners and dress properly.</b>

11:49.627 --> 11:51.547
<b>But that's not the case in Kamakura today.</b>

11:52.127 --> 11:55.717
<b>The Hojo fell,
and the Nitta's rule failed as well.</b>

11:55.797 --> 11:58.887
<b>The people no longer know
who their rightful ruler is.</b>

11:59.847 --> 12:03.847
<b>What Kamakura needs now
is youth and momentum.</b>

12:04.687 --> 12:09.277
<b>We must bring a breath of fresh air
and win the hearts of the weary people.</b>

12:10.937 --> 12:12.237
<b>People of Kamakura…</b>

12:12.777 --> 12:16.697
<b>Your peace will surely be protected by
the Ashikaga and the Hisashiban warriors!</b>

12:18.117 --> 12:20.827
<b>Glory to Kamakura!</b>

12:23.617 --> 12:24.917
<b>What a reception!</b>

12:24.997 --> 12:25.997
<b>HISASHIBAN MERCHANDISE STAND</b>

12:26.077 --> 12:28.627
<b>I hear even Ashikaga hand towels
are selling like crazy</b>

12:28.707 --> 12:30.377
<b>at the Hisashiban merchandise stand.</b>

12:32.217 --> 12:36.297
<b>How frightening.
What a pair of fearsome brothers.</b>

12:37.137 --> 12:40.137
<b>Lord Takauji wins people over
with his charisma,</b>

12:40.217 --> 12:42.977
<b>while Lord Tadayoshi wins them over
through calculation.</b>

12:43.477 --> 12:45.517
<b>Though their talents and methods
are completely different,</b>

12:45.597 --> 12:47.897
<b>they achieve exactly the same result.</b>

12:48.397 --> 12:50.317
<b>Tadayoshi Ashikaga!</b>

12:51.937 --> 12:53.817
<b>Your head is mine!</b>

12:55.777 --> 12:57.947
<b>Honma and Shibuya, is it? Admirable.</b>

12:58.027 --> 13:02.327
<b>You haven't forgotten your loyalty to
the Hojo, and you've come to avenge them.</b>

13:03.327 --> 13:04.617
<b>Huh?</b>

13:08.917 --> 13:10.207
<b>More are coming.</b>

13:10.297 --> 13:13.917
<b>Let's see… What? Only about 50?</b>

13:14.007 --> 13:16.087
<b>No. I think reinforcements are coming.</b>

13:16.887 --> 13:18.887
<b>They rang the bell
at the beginning, didn't they?</b>

13:18.967 --> 13:20.557
<b>If it were only a signal
for this many men,</b>

13:20.637 --> 13:22.807
<b>they wouldn't have needed
a bell that loud.</b>

13:22.887 --> 13:26.347
<b>They probably stationed
armored warriors nearby</b>

13:26.437 --> 13:29.227
<b>and planned to call them in
if the assassination failed.</b>

13:29.307 --> 13:30.317
<b>KOBUKUROZAKA PASS</b>

13:30.397 --> 13:31.647
<b>The only place close enough
to hear the bell and still hide an army</b>

13:31.727 --> 13:32.727
<b>is Kobukurozaka.</b>

13:32.817 --> 13:33.817
<b>MOAT
CURRENT LOCATION</b>

13:33.897 --> 13:35.317
<b>I thought something like this
might happen…</b>

13:35.397 --> 13:37.907
<b>We dug a moat there in case something like
this happened. We can hold them there.</b>

13:37.987 --> 13:43.037
<b>Understood. Iwamatsu and I
will handle the enemy there.</b>

13:43.117 --> 13:44.117
<b>Heck, yeah!</b>

13:44.747 --> 13:47.037
<b>Then I'll deal with
the enemy in front of us.</b>

13:47.877 --> 13:50.537
<b>My family were court nobles
until my grandfather's generation,</b>

13:50.627 --> 13:52.087
<b>so I'm a bit of a coward.</b>

13:52.167 --> 13:54.547
<b>I always keep a respectable force
close at hand.</b>

13:55.127 --> 13:58.047
<b>Oh, how frightening.</b>

13:58.637 --> 14:02.637
<b>Very well. I'll stay here and finish
the rest of my administrative duties.</b>

14:03.137 --> 14:04.927
<b>Try not to be too noisy.</b>

14:05.677 --> 14:06.807
<b>As you command.</b>

14:06.887 --> 14:08.267
<b>NEAR KOBUKUROZAKA ENTRANCE</b>

14:08.347 --> 14:10.017
<b>When did they build this?</b>

14:10.107 --> 14:13.607
<b>Rally the men!
We'll go around and cross the bridge!</b>

14:14.187 --> 14:15.187
<b>Those are…</b>

14:19.157 --> 14:21.067
<b>Shibukawa and Iwamatsu!</b>

14:21.157 --> 14:23.407
<b>Of all people, why are they here?</b>

14:26.037 --> 14:28.417
<b>Stay calm.
They can't reach us from that far away.</b>

14:31.127 --> 14:36.757
<b>From that distance?</b>

14:37.257 --> 14:41.757
<b>This is too one-sided. It's no fun.
Let's cross the bridge, Iwamatsu.</b>

14:42.257 --> 14:43.597
<b>Got it!</b>

14:46.727 --> 14:48.097
<b>How frightening.</b>

14:48.187 --> 14:51.807
<b>I almost feel sorry for anyone who has to
face down Mr. Shibukawa and Mr. Iwamatsu.</b>

14:52.357 --> 14:54.727
<b>Those two are monsters.</b>

14:55.227 --> 14:59.027
<b>But to me, Lord Tadayoshi is
still the most frightening.</b>

14:59.657 --> 15:00.657
<b>Look at that.</b>

15:03.907 --> 15:06.747
<b>He's positioned
just outside their arrow range.</b>

15:07.497 --> 15:09.667
<b>Has the unrest in Otawa Manor
not been quelled yet?</b>

15:10.207 --> 15:12.377
<b>Yoshiyuki's forces are strong.</b>

15:12.877 --> 15:16.547
<b>Rokuzaemon is an opportunist.
Send troops to intimidate him.</b>

15:16.627 --> 15:17.627
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

15:17.707 --> 15:20.627
<b>It appears the landholdings of the Seven
Warrior Groups of Musashi are unsettled…</b>

15:20.717 --> 15:23.637
<b>We're told there are so many marshes
that it's hardly fit to live in.</b>

15:23.717 --> 15:26.847
<b>Then tell them a decision will be made
after an on-site inspection.</b>

15:26.927 --> 15:27.927
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

15:28.017 --> 15:30.347
<b>And the plans
for Prince Nariyoshi's new residence?</b>

15:30.437 --> 15:31.557
<b>Here.</b>

15:31.647 --> 15:33.687
<b>Make it in the Kyo style.
I'll see to it tomorrow.</b>

15:33.767 --> 15:37.857
<b>It's not courage or bluff.
Everything has already been calculated.</b>

15:37.937 --> 15:43.117
<b>And he's only 27,
yet he has the power to shape the nation.</b>

15:43.197 --> 15:44.277
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

15:44.367 --> 15:46.577
<b>Magojiro, look to your right.
We're being pushed back.</b>

15:46.657 --> 15:47.657
<b>Yes, sir!</b>

15:48.657 --> 15:51.707
<b>As for anyone else I'd call frightening,
probably Mr. Imagawa.</b>

15:51.787 --> 15:53.877
<b>ASSISTANT, KANTO HISASHIBAN
NORIMITSU IMAGAWA</b>

15:53.957 --> 15:56.377
<b>I just can't get myself to tease him
about that mask.</b>

15:56.457 --> 15:57.667
<b>I know exactly what you mean.</b>

15:57.747 --> 16:00.717
<b>Someone who gives off that kind of vibe
is frightening.</b>

16:00.797 --> 16:03.637
<b>I've finished
my administrative duties as well.</b>

16:04.137 --> 16:05.547
<b>Shall we get something to eat, gentlemen?</b>

16:05.637 --> 16:07.307
<b>With pleasure.</b>

16:07.387 --> 16:08.847
<b>I'm starving.</b>

16:09.557 --> 16:12.387
<b>You are back already?</b>

16:12.477 --> 16:14.397
<b>That was all calculated too, wasn't it?</b>

16:15.647 --> 16:18.357
<b>If you hadn't made it back,
I was planning to leave without you.</b>

16:18.437 --> 16:22.277
<b><i>Tadayoshi Ashikaga, who laid the</i>
<i>foundation for the Muromachi shogunate…</i></b>

16:22.357 --> 16:23.857
<b><i>Through his skillful leadership,</i></b>

16:23.947 --> 16:28.157
<b><i>Kamakura was steadily being transformed</i>
<i>into a city under Ashikaga rule.</i></b>

16:28.237 --> 16:29.077
<b>KYO</b>

16:29.157 --> 16:30.157
<b><i>Meanwhile, in Kyo…</i></b>

16:30.247 --> 16:32.077
<b>The land that was promised to us…</b>

16:32.157 --> 16:33.367
<b>COURT OF CIVIL PETITIONS
CIVIL COURT ESTABLISHED BY EMPEROR GODAIGO</b>

16:33.457 --> 16:34.627
<b>…has been taken over by outsiders.</b>

16:34.707 --> 16:37.667
<b>We have nowhere left to live.
What are we supposed to do?</b>

16:37.747 --> 16:40.007
<b>Figure it out yourselves.</b>

16:40.087 --> 16:42.627
<b>I'm sick of hearing the same
kinds of complaints over and over.</b>

16:42.717 --> 16:45.337
<b><i>The Kenmu Restoration,</i>
<i>Emperor Godaigo's reform administration…</i></b>

16:45.427 --> 16:47.217
<b>ASHIKAGA STEWARD
MORONAO OF KO</b>

16:47.297 --> 16:49.307
<b><i>…was beginning to unravel.</i></b>

16:49.387 --> 16:54.647
<b><i>The Emperor generously rewarded</i>
<i>his favored nobles and warriors,</i></b>

16:54.727 --> 16:57.227
<b><i>but most warriors were either neglected</i>
<i>or left to fend for themselves.</i></b>

16:57.727 --> 16:59.897
<b><i>The people quickly grew disillusioned.</i></b>

17:00.647 --> 17:01.857
<b>MORONAO OF KO'S RESIDENCE</b>

17:01.937 --> 17:03.357
<b>That judicial system is a joke.</b>

17:03.447 --> 17:07.027
<b>The procedures are too complicated,
and no one follows the rulings.</b>

17:07.617 --> 17:10.907
<b>Anyone who refuses to obey
should simply be executed.</b>

17:10.987 --> 17:14.917
<b>No one would follow a ruling
unless it's backed by military force.</b>

17:14.997 --> 17:16.417
<b>MORONAO'S YOUNGER BROTHER
MOROYASU OF KO</b>

17:16.497 --> 17:18.917
<b>So only the strongest warrior
has the right to judge, eh?</b>

17:19.627 --> 17:22.337
<b>Then that certainly excludes the Emperor.</b>

17:22.417 --> 17:26.797
<b>The Emperor intends to raise taxes
to build a new grand palace.</b>

17:26.887 --> 17:28.887
<b>What a joke.</b>

17:28.967 --> 17:32.467
<b>Discontent is sweeping across the country
over the unequal rewards,</b>

17:32.557 --> 17:34.307
<b>and now he wants to raise taxes?</b>

17:35.057 --> 17:38.187
<b><i>The Emperor's new government</i>
<i>has progressive policies,</i></b>

17:38.267 --> 17:41.067
<b><i>but it's riddled with inefficiency</i>
<i>and is out of touch with reality.</i></b>

17:41.147 --> 17:42.107
<b><i>On the other hand,</i></b>

17:42.187 --> 17:45.317
<b><i>the Kamakura shogunate's</i>
<i>system of government was practical,</i></b>

17:45.397 --> 17:47.987
<b><i>but it could not adapt</i>
<i>to the changing times.</i></b>

17:48.527 --> 17:53.117
<b><i>We Ashikaga will simply take</i>
<i>the best from both.</i></b>

17:53.747 --> 17:56.207
<b><i>Right now in Kamakura,</i></b>

17:56.287 --> 17:58.457
<b><i>Lord Tadayoshi is learning</i>
<i>from the Kamakura shogunate's officials,</i></b>

17:58.537 --> 18:00.127
<b><i>taking in all their strengths.</i></b>

18:00.747 --> 18:05.007
<b>If we then add the experience and lessons
we gained from governing Kyo,</b>

18:05.087 --> 18:08.257
<b>a system of government for a new era
will be complete.</b>

18:08.337 --> 18:11.757
<b>Everything is for our lord, Lord Takauji.</b>

18:12.467 --> 18:13.767
<b>-Aye!
-Aye!</b>

18:13.847 --> 18:19.897
<b><i>While the Ashikaga retainers were</i>
<i>solidifying their vision for a new era…</i></b>

18:23.357 --> 18:24.857
<b>Seize him at once!</b>

18:29.567 --> 18:32.157
<b><i>Prince Moriyoshi,</i>
<i>Takauji's greatest opponent,</i></b>

18:32.237 --> 18:38.667
<b><i>was falsely accused of treason</i>
<i>and arrested by order of the Emperor.</i></b>

18:45.417 --> 18:47.167
<b>I hear I'm to be sent
to a prison in Kamakura,</b>

18:47.257 --> 18:48.717
<b>into the hands of your younger brother.</b>

18:49.587 --> 18:55.387
<b>Everything is unfolding
exactly as you intended.</b>

18:55.467 --> 18:59.017
<b>I can only regret
that it has come to this.</b>

18:59.727 --> 19:04.527
<b>Takauji, there is a way to achieve reform
in the safest possible way.</b>

19:04.607 --> 19:07.897
<b>It is to become the second reformer.</b>

19:09.317 --> 19:12.657
<b><i>Let the first reformer</i>
<i>destroy the old world.</i></b>

19:13.237 --> 19:14.237
<b>LIU</b>

19:14.327 --> 19:17.577
<b><i>Then overthrow the first reformer,</i>
<i>who has borne the people's resentment.</i></b>

19:17.657 --> 19:19.407
<b><i>Their resentment will be appeased,</i></b>

19:19.497 --> 19:21.327
<b><i>and the old world</i>
<i>will already have been destroyed.</i></b>

19:21.997 --> 19:25.247
<b>Then you can shape a new world
without any encumbrances.</b>

19:27.007 --> 19:29.167
<b>When you brought down
the Kamakura Shogunate,</b>

19:29.257 --> 19:32.297
<b>you could have simply
taken it over yourself.</b>

19:33.347 --> 19:34.757
<b>But you did not.</b>

19:34.847 --> 19:38.227
<b>Instead, you, first, handed everything
over to the first reformer.</b>

19:38.307 --> 19:42.057
<b>Your plan was to claim everything
as the second reformer.</b>

19:42.687 --> 19:44.477
<b>Am I wrong, Takauji?</b>

19:44.567 --> 19:47.647
<b>Give me everything. Everything!</b>

19:48.397 --> 19:51.317
<b>You might call it a greedy demon.</b>

19:52.317 --> 19:55.077
<b>It keeps crying out within me.</b>

19:56.197 --> 19:57.537
<b>But rest assured.</b>

19:58.657 --> 20:00.907
<b>My loyalty is genuine.</b>

20:00.997 --> 20:02.917
<b>As long as no great upheaval breaks out,</b>

20:02.997 --> 20:05.587
<b>I will spend my life
as the Emperor's loyal subject.</b>

20:06.917 --> 20:09.627
<b>As long as no great upheaval breaks out…</b>

20:13.137 --> 20:14.887
<b><i>There's certainty in his eyes.</i></b>

20:15.597 --> 20:17.967
<b><i>He knows that, under the Emperor's rule,</i>
<i>sooner or later,</i></b>

20:18.057 --> 20:19.807
<b><i>a great upheaval will break out.</i></b>

20:20.517 --> 20:22.687
<b><i>When that time comes,</i></b>

20:22.767 --> 20:25.437
<b><i>the demon within him</i>
<i>will reveal itself in full.</i></b>

20:27.767 --> 20:28.857
<b>OGASAWARA RESIDENCE, SHINANO</b>

20:28.937 --> 20:31.397
<b><i>Meanwhile, in the Ogasawara territory</i>
<i>in northwestern Shinano,</i></b>

20:31.487 --> 20:34.067
<b><i>the next move was already taking shape.</i></b>

20:34.157 --> 20:38.577
<b><i>As Shinano governor,</i>
<i>the mission Lord Takauji entrusted to me</i></b>

20:38.657 --> 20:42.957
<b><i>was to establish Ashikaga influence</i>
<i>throughout Shinano.</i></b>

20:43.037 --> 20:48.247
<b><i>And to track down the Hojo remnants</i>
<i>hiding in Shinano.</i></b>

20:48.997 --> 20:51.417
<b>I still have no proof.</b>

20:51.507 --> 20:55.137
<b>But my eyes have already given me a clue.</b>

20:55.217 --> 20:57.927
<b>Ever since that brat
got the better of me last year,</b>

20:58.007 --> 21:01.767
<b>he's been showing up at important events
far too often to be a coincidence.</b>

21:01.847 --> 21:06.477
<b>Yes. They disrupted the
provincial official's campaign as well.</b>

21:06.557 --> 21:09.687
<b>The men say
they call themselves the Elusive Warriors.</b>

21:10.527 --> 21:11.687
<b>Elusive? Like spies!?</b>

21:11.777 --> 21:12.777
<b>SPY WARRIORS</b>

21:12.857 --> 21:13.737
<b>CHOJA = SPY</b>

21:13.817 --> 21:16.487
<b>That's about as subtle as it gets!
What a ridiculous name!</b>

21:16.567 --> 21:22.747
<b>According to my spies, that brat was
taken in by Suwa Grand Shrine last year.</b>

21:22.827 --> 21:25.747
<b>Given the timing,
he's even more suspicious.</b>

21:25.827 --> 21:27.997
<b>That breeding is out of place
in the backwoods of Shinano.</b>

21:28.087 --> 21:29.587
<b>IMPORTANT RETAINERS
WARRIORS, FOOT SOLDIERS</b>

21:29.667 --> 21:32.167
<b>In my estimation, that brat is
either a member of the Hojo clan</b>

21:32.257 --> 21:34.007
<b>or the son
of one of its important retainers.</b>

21:34.587 --> 21:36.127
<b>For Yorishige, who took him in,</b>

21:36.217 --> 21:39.427
<b>a well-bred child from a distinguished
family would make the perfect spy.</b>

21:39.507 --> 21:42.807
<b>I believe he's been using the boy
while letting him gain experience.</b>

21:56.357 --> 21:58.317
<b><i>Bring him here for questioning.</i></b>

21:58.407 --> 22:01.157
<b><i>These eyes of mine</i>
<i>will see right through him!</i></b>

23:33.287 --> 23:34.917
<b>ASAKI YUIKAWA AS TOKIYUKI HOJO</b>

23:38.917 --> 23:39.927
<b><i>Let's go!</i></b>
